sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor P0 as Administrator
    participant P1 as Web Application (System)
    participant P2 as MetaAnalyticsController
    participant P3 as Queue Worker SyncMetaInsights / MetaInsights
    participant P4 as Application Database
    participant P5 as Meta Graph API
    P0->>P1: select accounts or request synchronization
    alt [change selected accounts]
    P1->>P2: PUT /admin/analytics/meta (connection_ids)
    P2->>P4: validate owned connections, one account per platform
    P4-->>P2: return validated connections
    P2->>P4: transaction: update analytics_settings, insert setting change
    P4-->>P2: commit configuration
    else [manual refresh]
    P1->>P2: POST /admin/analytics/meta/sync
    P2->>P2: authorize administrator, apply route throttle
    end
    P2->>P3: dispatch SyncMetaInsights (unique job)
    P2-->>P1: redirect back
    P1-->>P0: display current saved metrics
    P3->>P4: read selected social_connections
    P4-->>P3: return configured connections
    loop [each selected connection]
    alt [connection is disconnected]
    P3->>P4: set insights_status = disconnected
    else [connection is usable]
    P3->>P5: GET account insights (daily metrics, last 7 days)
    P5-->>P3: return metric series / provider error
    alt [valid points and same account/token still selected]
    P3->>P4: transaction: lock connection, recheck identity, upsert snapshots
    P3->>P4: set insights_status = ready and insights_synced_at
    P4-->>P3: commit snapshots
    else [no data / failure / changed connection]
    P3->>P4: set no_data or unavailable, discard stale-account response
    end
    end
    end
    Note over P0,P5: A later analytics request reads these snapshots. Queue timing depends on the configured driver, with a sync driver, dispatch runs inline. No automatic UI polling is implied.
